r of that i mean  you know  fanzines i don't know what their modern  equivalent is there must be things on  the internets but the old dittoed  fanzines and mimicry fans in my youth  were  a great and important part in my  development  not only me but of many many young  writers  and comic fans at the time  today fan fiction has come to mean  something very different it's come to  mean  taking the characters from an  established franchise like star wars or  star trek or  harry potter and writing original  stories of that i'm i'm not in favor of  that i'm you know it's  it's a copyright violation and uh  i don't think it's particularly good for  the franchises to have this kind of uh  derivative fiction out there and and i  don't think it's  good for the people writing it if they  aspire to be writers i mean  to be a writer you you need certainly to  master storytelling and prose but you  also need to master world building  and character creation if you're  borrowing all your characters and you're  borrowing the world  you're never gonna you're never gonna  get those aspects of your craft and and  be able to arrive at the point where you  can  create your own worlds and create your  own stories
 

